# Phase Delivery Hardening Standard

When generating phase delivery packages (START-HERE.md) for developers, ALWAYS include these safety mechanisms:

## 1. Single Session — No Session Restart

Phases run in ONE chat session to minimize request consumption. Use in-session Context Refresh to maintain quality.

## 2. Gate Checkpoint Protocol

Every phase with 6+ milestones MUST be organized in gates (max 5-6 milestones per gate). Between gates:
- Full test suite must pass with 0 failures
- Both backend and frontend must build without errors
- Golden path smoke test (3 core flows) must pass
- ALL prior gate ACs must be re-verified (cumulative)
- Changed files must be reviewed for scope creep
- dev-log.md must be updated with gate status
- Context Refresh must be executed

## 3. In-Session Context Refresh

At every gate boundary, the AI MUST:
1. Re-read `project-rules.md` using the Read tool
2. Re-read the NEXT gate's scope section
3. Re-read `dev-log.md`
4. Output the NON-NEGOTIABLES block
5. Output CURRENT STATE (5 lines: gate, commit, tests, risks, scope)

## 4. Mid-Gate Refresh (every 3 milestones)

After every 3rd milestone within a gate, do a lightweight refresh:
1. Re-read critical rules from project-rules.md
2. Re-read dev-log.md Current State
3. Output NON-NEGOTIABLES block

## 5. NON-NEGOTIABLES Block

Every START-HERE.md must begin with a 5-7 bullet NON-NEGOTIABLES block. This block is REPEATED before each gate section to survive context pressure.

## 6. Per-Milestone Self-Check (5-point)

Before every milestone commit, the AI must:
1. List satisfied AC IDs from scope doc
2. Name 3 earlier ACs at regression risk and verify them
3. Run tests — confirm no NEW failures
4. Flag any files modified outside milestone scope
5. Add dev-log.md entry

## 7. dev-log.md

Every phase generates a running dev-log.md with:
- Current state (active gate, last milestone, test count, build status)
- Per-milestone entries (what was done, tests, regression risks)
- Per-gate summaries (test counts, AC status, problems)
